.TH iapws 1 "15 August 2026" "0.7.1" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
iapws \- compute light and heavy water properties


.SH SYNOPSIS
.B iapws 
\fISUBCOMMAND\fP [\fIOPTION\fP]\.\.\.


.SH DESCRIPTION
.B iapws 
is a command line interface for computing properties
of light and heavy water according to IAPWS.

.SH SUBCOMMANDS
Valid subcommands are:
.RS
.TP
.B
+ kh
Compute the Henry's constant for gases in H2O or D2O.
The default behavior is to compute the constant kH for O2
at 25°C.See options.
See options.
.TP
.B
+ kd
Compute the vapor-liquid distribution constant for gases
in H2O or D2O.
The default behavior is to compute the constant kD for H2
at 25°C.
See options.
.TP
.B
+ psat
Compute the saturation pressure.
The default behavior is to compute psat at 25°C.
See options.
.TP
.B
+ Tsat
Compute the saturation temperature.
The default behavior is to compute Tsat at 1 bar.
See options.
.TP
.B
+ wp
Compute water properties for regions 1 to 5.
The default behavior is to compute the properties
at 25°C and 1 bar.
WARNING: Currently, only region 1 is supported.
.RE

.SH OPTIONS
.PP
kh:
.RS
.TP
.B
\fB-T\fP, \fB--temperature\fPTEMPERATURE\.\.\.
Temperature in °C. Default to 25°C.
.TP
.B
\fB-f\fP, \fB--fugacity\fP FUGACITY\.\.\.
Liquid-phase fugacity in MPa.
Default to 1 bar.
.TP
.B
\fB-g\fP, \fB--gases\fP GAS\.\.\.
Gases for which to compute kH.
Default to O2.
.TP
.B
\fB--D2O\fP
Set heavywater as the solvent.
.TP
.B
\fB--listgases\fP
Display available gases for
computing kH.
.RE
.PP
kd:
.RS
.TP
.B
\fB-T\fP, \fB--temperature\fP TEMPERATURE\.\.\.
Temperature in °C. Default to 25°C.
.TP
.B
\fB-x\fP, \fB--x2\fP x2\.\.\.
Molar fraction of gas in water.
Default to 1e-9.
.TP
.B
\fB-g\fP, \fB--gases\fP GAS\.\.\.
Gases for which to compute kD.
Default to H2.
.TP
.B
\fB--D2O\fP,
Set heavywater as the solvent.
.TP
.B
\fB--listgases\fP
Display available gases for
computing kD.
.RE
.PP
psat:
.RS
.TP
.B
\fB-T\fP, \fB--temperature\fP TEMPERATURE\.\.\.
Temperature in °C. Default to 25°C.
.RE
.PP
Tsat:
.RS
.TP
.B
 \fB-p\fP, \fB--pressure\fP PRESSURE\.\.\.
Pressure in bar. Default to 1 bar.
.RE
.PP
wp:
.RS
.TP
.B
\fB-T\fP, \fB--temperature\fP TEMPERATURE\.\.\.
Temperature in °C. Default to 25°C.
.TP
.B
\fB-p\fP, \fB--pressure\fP PRESSURE\.\.\.
Pressure in bar. Default to 1 bar.
.RE
.PP
all:
.RS
.TP
.B
\fB-u\fP, \fB--usage\fP
Show usage text and exit.
.TP
.B
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP,
Show help text and exit.
.TP
.B
\fB-v\fP, \fB--version\fP
Show version information and exit.
.SH NOTES

You may replace the default options from a file if your first
options begin with @file.
Initial options will then be read from the "response file"
"file.rsp" in the current directory.
.PP
If "file" does not exist or cannot be read, then an error occurs and
the program stops. Each line of the file is prefixed with "options"
and interpreted as a separate argument. The file itself may not
contain @file arguments. That is, it is not processed recursively.
.PP
For more information on response files see
https://urbanjost.github.io/M_CLI2/set_args.3m_cli2.html
.SH EXAMPLE
Minimal example
.PP
.nf
.ft CR
      iapws kh -T 25,100 -f 1,0.2 -g O2,H2
      iapws kd -T 25,100 -x2 1d-9,1d-6 -g O2,H2
      iapws wp -T 25,100 -p 0.035,1.0

.ft R
.fi

